Spec: LibScanHarbor

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  List every image repository of a Harbor project as `registry/name` image strings for the
    box-scan lane, authenticating either with an on-cluster dockerconfigjson pull secret or
    with Harbor's anonymous registry token.

Exposes:
  @list_repository(spec, namespace) — the module's sole @fn; reached by importers as
    `harbor::list_repository(...)` (the `import "scan_harbor" as harbor` convention; sole
    importer ./../boxes/scan.rhai, harbor-source lane only). Returns an @Array of strings.

Accepts:
  @spec — a @JukeBoxSpec-shaped @rhai::Dynamic (real `box.spec` through @JukeBox::get_spec, or
    a raw mock fixture map). Indexes `source.harbor.registry` and `source.harbor.project` (the
    @JukeBoxDef::Harbor variant of ./../../../common/src/jukebox.sdd) and reads the optional
    `pull_secret` key (@JukeBoxSpec::pull_secret, dockerconfigjson secret name).
  @namespace — @String namespace owning the pull Secret (the scan lane passes
    `args.namespace`); unused when the anonymous branch runs.
  A bare-host `registry` index — the scheme is hardcoded and the client base URL is built
    `https://${registry}`.

Returns:
  An @Array of `${registry}/${p.name}` strings, one per repository row across all pages:
    page 1 mapped first, each later page extended in with @Array.append — order is Harbor's
    `sort=name` page order, no dedup, no filter. The string is the "image string" convention
    the importer re-splits on its first `/`.

Raises:
  @throw `Cannot get anonymous authentication from harbor` — static text, HTTP code not
    interpolated — when the token exchange answers any `code` other than `200`.
  @throw `Unable to list from ${registry}/${project}` when the initial list page or any
    later page answers any `code` other than `200` — the loop and the initial request throw
    the identical interpolated text; neither the page number nor the code appears in it.
  Engine errors, uncaught — the file mints no guard of its own so each reaches the caller:
    @secret::get_auth_from raising per ./secret_dockerconfigjson.sdd; @parse_int over a
    non-integer `x-total-count` text; the missing-header case where @headers_get returns `()`
    and @parse_int has no @() candidate; a token answer without `token` making
    @add_header_bearer receive `()`; a non-JSON list body arriving as `#{}` where `.map`
    fails; a row without `name`.

Handles:
  No `pull_secret` key, or the key present as the empty string — the anonymous token branch.
  A single-page project (`x-total-count` up to `10`) or an empty project (`0`) — the loop
    runs no iteration and only the page-1 answer is mapped.

Must:
  Build exactly one @new_http_client(`https://${registry}`) reused for the token and all list
    requests; every path given to @get is relative (base-join owned by the core client).
  Authenticate through exactly one exclusive branch keyed on
    `"pull_secret" in spec.keys() && spec.pull_secret!=""`: the secret branch calls
    @secret::get_auth_from(spec.pull_secret, @namespace, @registry) — the exact credential
    triple frozen by ./secret_dockerconfigjson.sdd — and applies @add_header_basic(auth.user,
    auth.pass); the else branch issues the anonymous GET
    `service/token?service=harbor-registry&scope=repository:${project}/*:pull` before any
    header is set on the client, then @add_header_bearer(auth.json.token). The secret branch
    never calls the token endpoint; the bearer is never set on failure.
  Fetch page one with GET `api/v2.0/projects/${project}/repositories?page_size=10&sort=name`
    — no `page` param, Harbor serves page one — and page `i` with GET
    `api/v2.0/projects/${project}/repositories?page=${i}&page_size=10&sort=name`, param order
    verbatim.
  Compute the page budget as `max_size = @parse_int(@headers_get(initial.headers, "x-total-count"))`
    then `max_pages = @to_int(@ceiling(max_size / 10.0)) + 1` — INT over the float literal
    divides to FLOAT, @ceiling is the FLOAT whole-up, @to_int truncates the whole-valued
    FLOAT back to INT — and loop `for i in 2..max_pages` with its endpoint exclusive: fetched
    pages are exactly `2` through `ceil(max_size / 10)`, the true last page, so page 1 is
    never re-fetched and no page beyond the last is requested. The `10.0` divisor and the
    `page_size=10` query param are one constant and must move together (drift silently skips
    or refetches pages).

Depends on:
  ./secret_dockerconfigjson.sdd — imported at line 1 as `secret`; @secret::get_auth_from is
    the whole secret branch and its raise propagates untouched.
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — @new_http_client, @add_header_basic, @add_header_bearer,
    @get (the client's `#{code, headers, body, json}` result, `code` an INT) and the free
    @headers_get (case-insensitive, `()` when absent), real @http_rhai_register on scan
    engines and the mock twin on mock engines, both wired per
    ./../../../common/src/rhaihandler.sdd.
  The locked rhai default math package behind @vynil_core::engine::Script::new_bare —
    @parse_int, @ceiling, @to_int — plus range `for`.

References:
  ./../boxes/scan.rhai — sole importer; its harbor `spec.source` key routes here, and this
    return shape feeds its first-`/` registry/repository split and @new_registry tag scan.
  ./../../../common/src/jukebox.sdd — the spec shape (`harbor` `{registry, project}`,
    `pull_secret` serialization).
  ./../../src/boxes/scan.sdd — the Rust lane that runs the importer script.
  ./../../tests/rhai_scan_gitlab.rs — nearest harness a harbor-lane test would mirror
    (wiremock + real http + mock k8s).

Scenario: pull_secret branch authenticates basic and skips the token endpoint
  Given a spec with `pull_secret` `harbor-pull`, `source.harbor` `{registry: harbor.example, project: apps}`
    and a Secret resolving to `{user, pass}` for `harbor.example`
  When @list_repository("...", "vynil-system") runs
  Then @secret::get_auth_from receives the secret name, the namespace and the bare host, the
    client carries @add_header_basic(auth.user, auth.pass), the token endpoint is never
    called, and the answer lists every row as `harbor.example/<name>`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: anonymous branch exchanges a project-wide pull token
  Given a spec with no `pull_secret` key
  When @list_repository runs
  Then GET `service/token?service=harbor-registry&scope=repository:apps/*:pull` is issued
    before any auth header, and `json.token` becomes @add_header_bearer
  But any `code` other than `200` throws the static `Cannot get anonymous authentication from harbor`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: fifteen rows paginate to exactly one follow-up page
  Given `x-total-count` `15` and pages of 10 and 5 rows
  Then `max_pages` is `to_int(ceiling(15 / 10.0)) + 1` = `3` and `2..3` fetches page 2 only —
    15 mapped strings, no page-3 request, page 1 not re-fetched
  But with `x-total-count` `0` the loop range is empty and the answer is `[]`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: missing x-total-count kills the scan on parse
  Given a `200` initial page whose headers carry no `x-total-count`
  Then @headers_get answers `()` and @parse_int has no `()` candidate — an engine error
    surfaces to the caller with no throw text of its own
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: any failing list page shares one message
  Given the initial list request or a loop page answering `404`
  Then @throw `Unable to list from harbor.example/apps` — the identical text whichever page
    failed, no code and no page number in it
  No mapped test exists.

Tasks:
  [ ] Add harbor-lane wiremock tests mirroring ./../../tests/rhai_scan_gitlab.rs (basic
      branch, anonymous branch plus token non-200, the 15-row and 20-row page edges, missing
      `x-total-count`, list 404). No file under ./../../tests/ references this module today;
      ./../../tests/rhai_scan.rs covers the filter/security lanes and ./../../tests/rhai_scan_http.rs
      the http/s3 lanes only.
  [?] The `pull_secret` null trap: @JukeBoxSpec::pull_secret is an @Option with no
      `skip_serializing_if`, so @JukeBox::get_spec always emits the key for real JukeBoxes —
      as `()` in rhai — and `()!=""` is true, sending a real pull-secret-less box down the
      @secret::get_auth_from branch to die on the `()` secret name; the anonymous branch is
      then only reachable from raw-fixture specs without the key. The importer's own
      `use_auth` guard additionally tests `!= ()`. Decide whether this guard aligns (or the
      Option serialization skips none).
  [?] Failure texts are thinner than the ./scan_gitlab.rhai sibling's (no HTTP code, no page
      number, and the initial-page and page-i failures are indistinguishable), so a
      multi-page incident lands in the box condition message undiagnosable. Decide later
      whether to enrich them.

Done when:
  The harbor-lane Scenarios above carry mapped wiremock tests, the `pull_secret` null guard
    decision is recorded, and the `${registry}/${name}` contract still matches what
    ./../boxes/scan.rhai splits.
